---
const skills = ['Java', 'Spring Boot', 'Redis', 'MySQL', 'Linux', 'Agent', 'Robots'];
---

<section class="py-20 border-t border-border reveal">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6">About</h2>
  <div class="space-y-4 text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
    <p>
      I build backend systems and care about what happens underneath them. Lately
      that means Redis — cache consistency, distributed locks, and the concurrency
      problems that only show up once real traffic arrives.
    </p>
    <p>
      I learn by taking things apart and rebuilding them. Following a system down to
      its data structures teaches me more than reading about it — and the interesting
      part is always the case where the textbook answer breaks.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-6">
    {skills.map((skill) => (
      <span class="bg-bg-card border border-border px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-sm text-text-muted">
        {skill}
      </span>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
